            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Bengali for to pant, then the Bengali for to groan."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: যন্ত্রণা",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "যন্ত্রণা — jôntrônā — \"agony; torment; severe pain\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "দাঁতের যন্ত্রণায় দাদু সারারাত জেগে ছিলেন। dā̃ter jôntrônāy dādu sārārāt jege chhilen. Grandfather lay awake all night in agony from his tooth."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ব্যথা (taught) is any pain; যন্ত্রণা (jôntrônā) is pain that torments, of the body or of the mind."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "যন্ত্রণা (jôntrônā) is a tatsama, Sanskrit yantraṇā, which Monier-Williams gives first for restraint and constraint and then for pain and anguish; Bengali keeps the pain."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
